Zakat is defined as a mandatory right in specific property for a specific group at a specific time [[qa:icadb:26088]]. It is one of the pillars of Islam and is characterized as a mandatory charity taken from the wealthy to be given to the poor [[qa:icadb:26088, qa:bayyinat:206]].

{{quran:98:5}}

Giving zakah is part of the correct religion [[quran:98:5]]. It serves various purposes and provides benefits to the giver, the needy recipients, and the community as a whole [[qa:bayyinat:206]].

{{quran:9:60}}

Allah has mandated that zakah expenditures be distributed among specific groups, including the poor, the needy, those employed for its distribution, those whose hearts are being reconciled [for Islam], freeing captives, those in debt, for the cause of Allah, and the stranded traveler [[quran:9:60]]. Regarding Zakat al-Fitr specifically, it is required from every Muslim, including slaves, free people, males, females, young, and old [[hadith:hadeethenc:4520]].

